    Carry the norm parameter table openings in the first norm message
    
    The first norm message gains the optional parameter table openings: the gain
    openings and, for a separate bias table, the bias openings, each carrying the
    position, salt, one symbol per table row and the Merkle path. The wire section
    is present only when the plan carries the parameter tables, so the existing
    norm messages are unchanged. The witness gains the private parameter vectors
    for the later relation rows. The parameter width now has to fit the usable
    plain message region of the table instead of the codeword length, and the
    opening codec enforces the reader's row count, code depth, salt length, column
    range and strictly increasing positions.
    
    partial progress

